<p>NPRR Photo October 1882 1907 RPPC of NP High Bridge</p>

<p>Work began on the bridge on September 1, 1881. The east approach span was finished May 9, 1882. The west approach span was completed June 3, 1882. The center span was completed October 18, 1882. The final cost was $1.08 million. Between 200 and 600 men worked on it at any given time, dependant on what aspects of the bridge were under construction.The first spans were flat topped but were replaced in 1905 when the loads which could be transported by improved locomotives exceeded the capacity of the initial design. The bridge trusses were rebuilt atop the existing piers using sturdier and elegant arc-topped spans which remain in service today.</p>

